t sbcCommaList\" data-group=\"armor\">  <li>+3 Natural</li>  <li>+1 Size</li>  </ul>  <br /><ul class=\"sbcSemicolonList\"><li><strong>Hit Points</strong> 18 (2 HD; 2d10+7)</li>  </ul><br /><ul class=\"sbcSemicolonList\"><li><ul class=\"sbcCommaList\" data-content=\"saves\"><li><strong>Fort</strong> +5</li><li><strong>Ref</strong> +0</li><li><strong>Will</strong> +3</li></ul></li>   </ul><br /><ul class=\"sbcSemicolonList\">   <li><strong>DR</strong><ul class=\"sbcCommaList\" data-content=\"dr\">  <li>5/Cold Iron or Good</li>  </ul></li>   <li><strong>Immune</strong><ul class=\"sbcCommaList\" data-content=\"immune\">  <li>Electricity</li>  <li>Poison</li>  </ul></li>   <li><strong>Resist</strong><ul class=\"sbcCommaList\" data-content=\"resist\">  <li>Acid 10</li>  <li>Cold 10</li>  <li>Fire 10</li>  </ul></li>    </ul>  </div><div><div class=\"sbcSection\" data-content=\"offense\"><h4>Offense</h4><hr /><strong>Speed</strong><ul class=\"sbcCommaList\" data-content=\"speed\">  <li>Land 20 ft</li>  </ul><br />  <strong>Melee</strong> 2 claws +4 (1d4+1), bite +4 (1d4+1)<br />   <ul class=\"sbcSemicolonList\">   </ul>   </div></div>  <div class=\"sbcSection\">  <div class=\"spellBook\"><strong>Spell-like abilities</strong><ul class=\"sbcParensWrappedList sbcSemicolonList\"><li>CL 2</li><li>Concentration +2</li>  </ul><ul class=\"sbcSpellList\">  <li>  1/Day  —<ul class=\"sbcCommaList sbcItalic\">  <li> Summon (level , 1 dretch 35%) <ul class=\"sbcParensWrappedList sbcCommaList\">   </ul></li>  <li> Cause Fear <ul class=\"sbcParensWrappedList sbcCommaList\">   <li>DC 11</li> </ul></li>  <li> Stinking Cloud <ul class=\"sbcParensWrappedList sbcCommaList\">   <li>DC 13</li> </ul></li>  </ul></li>   </ul></div>  </div>    <div class=\"sbcSection\" data-content=\"statistics\"><h4>Statistics</h4><hr /><ul class=\"sbcCommaList\" data-content=\"attributes\"><li><strong>Str</strong> 12</li><li><strong>Dex</strong> 10</li><li><strong>Con</strong> 14</li><li><strong>Int</strong> 5</li><li><strong>Wis</strong> 11</li><li><strong>Cha</strong> 11</li></ul><br /><ul class=\"sbcSemicolonList\" data-content=\"base-attack\"><li><strong>Base Atk</strong>+2</li><li><strong>CMB</strong> +2</li><li><strong>CMD</strong> 12  </li></ul><br />  <strong>Feats</strong><ul class=\"sbcCommaList\" data-content=\"feats\">  <li>Toughness</li>  </ul><br />   <strong>Skills</strong><ul class=\"sbcCommaList\" data-content=\"skills\">  <li>Escape Artist +5</li>  <li>Perception +5</li>  <li>Stealth +9</li>  </ul>  <br />   <strong>Languages</strong><ul class=\"sbcCommaList\" data-content=\"languages\">  <li>Abyssal (cannot speak)</li>  <li>telepathy 100 ft. (limited to Abyssal-speaking targets)</li>  </ul><br />    </div>  <div class=\"sbcSection\" data-content=\"ecology\"><h4>Ecology</h4><hr />  <strong>Environment</strong>   any (Abyss)<br />   <strong>Organization</strong>  solitary, pair, gang (3-5), crowd (6-12), or mob (13+)<br />   <strong>Treasure</strong>  none   <br />  </div>      <div class=\"sbcSection\" data-content=\"description\"><h4> Description </h4><hr /><div class=\"sbcPreWrap\">\nEven the lowest demons of the Abyss are dangerous and filled with a driving need to spread ruin and dismay. The lowly dretch is as hideous and foul as it is cruel, even if it lacks the strength and power to realize its need to brutalize others in its native realm.\n\nThe lot of the dretch's existence is to serve more powerful demons as victims, and only the lucky few survive long enough to evolve.\n\nThe dretch is a favorite target for dabblers in Abyssal summonings to call forth. Relatively weak and easy to bully, dretches can often be pressured into long periods of servitude with only vague promises of the opportunity to vent their frustrations and anger on softer foes. Yet the prospective dretch-summoner would do well to remember that these demons are as craven and untrustworthy as they come. A dretch faced with a more powerful foe is only too eager to trade what it knows for its pitiful excuse for a life.\n\nUnlike most demons, a dretch's slovenly personality and disdain for prolonged physical labor rarely result in success. Advanced dretches are rare, but those who do find it within themselves to be more than they were at creation often become the pauper-kings of the Abyss, cruel and bitter in their rule over vermin, broken souls, mindless undead, and other dretches. Their empires are confined to abandoned stretches of sewers under backwater cities, unstable reaches of swampland avoided by more sensible minds, and other undesirable corners of the Abyss that even demons find uncomfortable or foul.\n\nYet to the dretch lords, these realms are their empires, and they defend them with a pitiful tenacity.\n\nA dretch stands 4 feet tall and weighs 180 pounds.\n\nDretches typically form from the souls of slothful, evil mortals-yet it only takes a small fragment of a soul to trigger such a hideous birth. A single soul can often trigger the manifestation of a small army of dretches, and the sight of a horde of fresh-birthed dretches pulling free from the heaving protomatter of the Abyss is a nauseating and terrifying one indeed.\n</div></div>  </div><hr class=\"sbcBorder\" /></div><p></p></div><br /><hr /><div class=\"rawInputContainer\" style=\"margin-top:15px\"><h2 style=\"text-align:middle;border:none;text-transform:uppercase;color:#000\">RAW INPUT</h2><hr /><pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:14px\">    Dretch (CR 2)\nSource PFRPG Bestiary \nCR 2 \nXP 600 \nCE Small outsider (chaotic, demon, evil, extraplanar)\n\nInit +0; Senses darkvision 60 ft.; Perception +5   \nDefense   \nAC 14, touch 11, flat-footed 14 (+3 natural, +1 size)\n\nhp 18 (2d10+7)\n\nFort +5, Ref +0, Will +3 \nDR 5/cold iron or good; Immune electricity, poison; Resist acid 10, cold 10, fire 10   \nOffense   \nSpd 20 ft. \nMelee 2 claws +4 (1d4+1), bite +4 (1d4+1)\n\nSpell-like abilities (cl 2nd)\n\n1/day-cause fear (DC 11), stinking cloud (DC 13), summon (level 1, 1 dretch 35%)\n\n\n\nStatistics   \nStr 12, Dex 10, Con 14, Int 5, Wis 11, Cha 11 \nBase Atk +2; CMB +2; CMD 12 \nFeats Toughness \nSkills Escape Artist +5, Perception +5, Stealth +9 \nLanguages Abyssal (cannot speak); telepathy 100 ft. (limited to Abyssal-speaking targets)\n\n\n\nEcology   \nEnvironment  any (Abyss)\n\nOrganization solitary, pair, gang (3-5), crowd (6-12), or mob (13+)\n\nTreasure none   \nDescription\n\nEven the lowest demons of the Abyss are dangerous and filled with a driving need to spread ruin and dismay. The lowly dretch is as hideous and foul as it is cruel, even if it lacks the strength and power to realize its need to brutalize others in its native realm.\n\nThe lot of the dretch's existence is to serve more powerful demons as victims, and only the lucky few survive long enough to evolve.\n\nThe dretch is a favorite target for dabblers in Abyssal summonings to call forth. Relatively weak and easy to bully, dretches can often be pressured into long periods of servitude with only vague promises of the opportunity to vent their frustrations and anger on softer foes. Yet the prospective dretch-summoner would do well to remember that these demons are as craven and untrustworthy as they come. A dretch faced with a more powerful foe is only too eager to trade what it knows for its pitiful excuse for a life.\n\nUnlike most demons, a dretch's slovenly personality and disdain for prolonged physical labor rarely result in success. Advanced dretches are rare, but those who do find it within themselves to be more than they were at creation often become the pauper-kings of the Abyss, cruel and bitter in their rule over vermin, broken souls, mindless undead, and other dretches. Their empires are confined to abandoned stretches of sewers under backwater cities, unstable reaches of swampland avoided by more sensible minds, and other undesirable corners of the Abyss that even demons find uncomfortable or foul.\n\nYet to the dretch lords, these realms are their empires, and they defend them with a pitiful tenacity.\n\nA dretch stands 4 feet tall and weighs 180 pounds.\n\nDretches typically form from the souls of slothful, evil mortals-yet it only takes a small fragment of a soul to trigger such a hideous birth. A single soul can often trigger the manifestation of a small army of dretches, and the sight of a horde of fresh-birthed dretches pulling free from the heaving protomatter of the Abyss is a nauseating and terrifying one indeed.\n    </pre></div>"},"cr":{"base":2},"xp":{"value":0}},"skills":{"acr":{"ability":"dex","rt":false,"acp":true,"rank":0},"apr":{"ability":"int","rt":false,"acp":false,"rank":0},"art":{"ability":"int","rt":false,"acp":false,"rank":0},"blf":{"ability":"cha","rt":false,"acp":false,"rank":0},"clm":{"ability":"str","rt":false,"acp":true,"rank":0},"crf":{"ability":"int","rt":false,"acp":false,"rank":0},"dip":{"ability":"cha","rt":false,"acp":false,"rank":0},"dev":{"ability":"dex","rt":true,"acp":true,"rank":0},"dis":{"ability":"cha","rt":false,"acp":false,"rank":0},"esc":{"ability":"dex","rt":false,"acp":true,"rank":2},"fly":{"ability":"dex","rt":false,"acp":true,"rank":0},"han":{"ability":"cha","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"hea":{"ability":"wis","rt":false,"acp":false,"rank":0},"int":{"ability":"cha","rt":false,"acp":false,"rank":0},"kar":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"kdu":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"ken":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"kge":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"khi":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"klo":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"kna":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"kno":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"kpl":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"kre":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"lin":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"lor":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"per":{"ability":"wis","rt":false,"acp":false,"rank":2},"prf":{"ability":"cha","rt":false,"acp":false,"rank":0},"pro":{"ability":"wis","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"rid":{"ability":"dex","rt":false,"acp":true,"rank":0},"sen":{"ability":"wis","rt":false,"acp":false,"rank":0},"slt":{"ability":"dex","rt":true,"acp":true,"rank":0},"spl":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"ste":{"ability":"dex","rt":false,"acp":true,"rank":2},"sur":{"ability":"wis","rt":false,"acp":false,"rank":0},"swm":{"ability":"str","rt":false,"acp":true,"rank":0},"umd":{"ability":"cha","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0}},"traits":{"size":"sm","ageCategory":"adult","senses":{"dv":{"value":60},"ts":{"value":0},"bs":{"value":0},"bse":{"value":0},"ll":{"enabled":false,"multiplier":{"dim":2,"bright":2}},"ls":{"value":0},"sid":false,"tr":{"value":0},"si":false,"sc":{"value":0},"custom":""},"hardness":0,"dr":{"value":[{"amount":5,"types":["coldIron","good"],"operator":true}],"custom":""},"eres":{"value":[{"amount":10,"types":["acid"],"operator":false},{"amount":10,"types":["cold"],"operator":false},{"amount":10,"types":["fire"],"operator":false}],"custom":""},"cres":"","regen":"","fastHealing":"","languages":["Abyssal (cannot speak)","telepathy 100 ft. (limited to Abyssal-speaking targets)"],"di":["electric"],"dv":[],"ci":["poison"],"stature":"tall"},"currency":{"pp":0,"gp":0,"sp":0,"cp":0},"altCurrency":{"pp":0,"gp":0,"sp":0,"cp":0}},"prototypeToken":{"name":"Dretch","displayName":20,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/terror.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"offsetX":0,"offsetY":0,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"rotation":0,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":20,"bar1":{"attribute":"attributes.hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":null},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":true,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":[],"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[{"name":"Outsider","type":"race","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>An outsider is at least partially composed of the essence (but not necessarily the material) of some plane other than the Material Plane. Some creatures start out as some other type and become outsiders when they attain a higher (or lower) state of spiritual existence.</p>\n<h2>Features</h2>\n<p>An outsider has the following features.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>d10 Hit Dice.</li>\n<li>Base attack bonus equal to total Hit Dice (fast progression).</li>\n<li>Two good saving throws, usually <em>Reflex</em> and Will.</li>\n<li>Skill points equal to 6 + Int modifier (minimum 1) per Hit Die. The following are class skills for outsiders: <em>Bluff</em>, <em>Craft</em>, <em>Knowledge</em> (planes), <em>Perception</em>, <em>Sense Motive</em>, and <em>Stealth</em>. Due to their varied nature, outsiders also receive 4 additional class skills determined by the creature’s theme.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Traits</h2>\n<p>An outsider possesses the following traits (unless otherwise noted in a creature’s entry).</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Darkvision 60 feet.</li>\n<li>Unlike most living creatures, an outsider does not have a dual nature—its soul and body form one unit. When an outsider is slain, no soul is set loose. Spells that restore souls to their bodies, such as <em>raise dead</em>, <em>reincarnate</em>, and <em>resurrection</em>, don’t work on an outsider. It takes a different magical effect, such as <em>limited wish</em>, <em>wish</em>, <em>miracle</em>, or <em>true resurrection</em> to restore it to life. An outsider with the native subtype can be raised, reincarnated, or resurrected just as other living creatures can be.</li>\n<li>Proficient with all simple and martial weapons and any weapons mentioned in its entry.</li>\n<li>Proficient with whatever type of armor (light, medium, or heavy) it is described as wearing, as well as all lighter types. Outsiders not indicated as wearing armor are not proficient with armor. Outsiders are proficient with shields if they are proficient with any form of armor.</li>\n<li>Outsiders breathe, but do not need to eat or sleep (although they can do so if they wish). Native outsiders breathe, eat, and sleep.</li>\n</ul>","instructions":""},"tags":[],"changes":[],"changeFlags":{"immuneToMorale":false,"loseDexToAC":false,"noMediumEncumbrance":false,"noHeavyEncumbrance":false,"mediumArmorFullSpeed":false,"heavyArmorFullSpeed":false,"lowLightVision":false,"seeInvisibility":false,"seeInDarkness":false},"contextNotes":[],"links":{"children":[],"supplements":[]},"armorProf":[],"weaponProf":[],"languages":[],"flags":{"boolean":{},"dictionary":{}},"scriptCalls":[],"size":"sm","speeds":{"land":null,"fly":null,"flyManeuverability":"","swim":null,"climb":null,"burrow":null},"creatureTypes":["outsider"],"creatureSubtypes":["chaotic","demon","evil","extraplanar"],"sources":[{"id":"PZO1112","pages":"309"}]},"img":"systems/pf1/icons/skills/yellow_40.jpg","_id":"V2JqYpVrkaJtbDeg","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":112500,"flags":{},"_stats":{"coreVersion":"13.351","systemId":"pf1","systemVersion":"11.11","createdTime":1795124569121,"modifiedTime":1795124572308,"lastModifiedBy":"C7TQ7ZOKBUpwNi2A"},"ownership":{"default":0}},{"_id":"TwU7XNvn7QYqkU8z","_stats":{"coreVersion":"13.351","systemId":"pf1","systemVersion":"11.11","createdTime":1795124569183,"modifiedTime":1795124572308,"lastModifiedBy":"C7TQ7ZOKBUpwNi2A"},"img":"systems/pf1/icons/skills/yellow_40.jpg","name":"Outsider","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>An outsider is at least partially composed of the essence (but not necessarily the material) of some plane other than the Material Plane. Some creatures start out as some other type and become outsiders when they attain a higher (or lower) state of spiritual existence.</p>\n<h2>Features</h2>\n<p>An outsider has the following features.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>d10 Hit Dice.</li>\n<li>Base attack bonus equal to total Hit Dice (fast progression).</li>\n<li>Two good saving throws, usually <em>Reflex</em> and Will.</li>\n<li>Skill points equal to 6 + Int modifier (minimum 1) per Hit Die. The following are class skills for outsiders: <em>Bluff</em>, <em>Craft</em>, <em>Knowledge</em> (planes), <em>Perception</em>, <em>Sense Motive</em>, and <em>Stealth</em>. Due to their varied nature, outsiders also receive 4 additional class skills determined by the creature’s theme.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Traits</h2>\n<p>An outsider possesses the following traits (unless otherwise noted in a creature’s entry).</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Darkvision 60 feet.</li>\n<li>Unlike most living creatures, an outsider does not have a dual nature—its soul and body form one unit. When an outsider is slain, no soul is set loose. Spells that restore souls to their bodies, such as <em>raise dead</em>, <em>reincarnate</em>, and <em>resurrection</em>, don’t work on an outsider. It takes a different magical effect, such as <em>limited wish</em>, <em>wish</em>, <em>miracle</em>, or <em>true resurrection</em> to restore it to life. An outsider with the native subtype can be raised, reincarnated, or resurrected just as other living creatures can be.</li>\n<li>Proficient with all simple and martial weapons and any weapons mentioned in its entry.</li>\n<li>Proficient with whatever type of armor (light, medium, or heavy) it is described as wearing, as well as all lighter types. Outsiders not indicated as wearing armor are not proficient with armor. Outsiders are proficient with shields if they are proficient with any form of armor.</li>\n<li>Outsiders breathe, but do not need to eat or sleep (although they can do so if they wish). Native outsiders breathe, eat, and sleep.</li>\n</ul>","instructions":""},"tags":[],"changes":[],"changeFlags":{"immuneToMorale":false,"loseDexToAC":false,"noMediumEncumbrance":false,"noHeavyEncumbrance":false,"mediumArmorFullSpeed":false,"heavyArmorFullSpeed":false,"lowLightVision":false,"seeInvisibility":false,"seeInDarkness":false},"contextNotes":[],"links":{"children":[],"classAssociations":[],"supplements":[]},"tag":"outsider","armorProf":[],"weaponProf":["simple","martial"],"languages":[],"flags":{"boolean":{},"dictionary":{}},"scriptCalls":[],"subType":"racial","level":2,"hd":10,"hp":11,"bab":"high","skillsPerLevel":6,"savingThrows":{"fort":{"value":"high"},"ref":{"value":"low"},"will":{"value":"high"}},"fc":{"hp":{"value":0},"skill":{"value":0},"alt":{"value":0,"notes":""}},"wealth":"","alignment":"","classSkills":{"blf":true,"crf":true,"kpl":true,"per":true,"sen":true,"ste":true,"esc":true},"sources":[{"id":"PZO1112","pages":"309"}]},"type":"class","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":112500,"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.pf1.racial-hd.Item.cV7yHt8i5YCV0ZTd"}},"ownership":{"default":0}},{"_id":"WLC1In0T7oePaxFz","_stats":{"coreVersion":"13.351","systemId":"pf1","systemVersion":"11.11","createdTime":1795124569527,"modifiedTime":1795124572308,"lastModifiedBy":"C7TQ7ZOKBUpwNi2A"},"img":"systems/pf1/icons/feats/toughness.jpg","name":"Toughness","system":{"description":{"value":"<i>You have enhanced physical stamina.</i><p><strong>Benefits</strong>: You gain +3 hit points. For every Hit Die you possess beyond 3, you gain an additional +1 hit point. If you have more than 3 Hit Dice, you gain +1 hit points whenever you gain a Hit Die (such as when you gain a level).</p>","instructions":""},"tags":["General","Defensive"],"actions":[],"attackNo